*******************************************************************************
****************** VOLTUS FOUNDATION FLOW USAGE DETAILS **************************
*******************************************************************************
====================
Directory Structure:
====================
                VOLTUS_FF
	          |
	          +  README.VOLTUS (The file which you are looking at present)
	          |
                  +  TEMPLATES
                  |      |
		  |      \--- VOLTUS\
		  |		    |
	          |     	    +  setup.tcl  (Setting up the design file variables)
	          |     	    |
	          |                 \  voltus_config.tcl (Setting up the VOLTUS FLOW related variables)
	          |      
	          +  PLUG/VOLTUS (Contains VOLTUS PLUG-IN scripts)
	          |
	          +  EXAMPLES (Contains in-house design example)
	          |	|
	          |	\--- VOLTUS\
		  |	           |
		  |	           +  setup.tcl (Modified as per this design requirement)
	          |                |
	          |	           \  voltus_config.tcl (Modified as per this design requirement)
	          |		
	          +  SCRIPTS  (VOLTUS FF Scripts)
	          |	|
	          |	+  gen_voltus_flow.tcl (This generates VOLTUS script to run the Flow)
	          |	|
	          |     +--- VOLTUS\ (This contains VOLTUS flow required scripts)
	          |	|
	          |	\--- ETC\
	          |             |
	          |	        \ VOLTUS (VOLTUS supporting scripts)
                  |                |
                  |                + utils.tcl (The voltus supporting procs)
                  |                |
                  |                + default_settings.tcl (The voltus flow default settings)
                  |                |
                  |                \ check_setup.tcl (The check the variables entered in VOLTUS FF setup/voltus_config files)
	          |
(Code Gen O/P)    +  Makefile  (The make file used to run the VOLTUS Analysis through Foundation Flow)
	          |
(Code Gen O/P)    +  FF  (Contains the flattened VOLTUS Flow scripts generated by Code Generator)
	          |   |
	          |   +  voltus.check.rpt (The setup check report)
	          |   |
	          |   \--- VOLTUS
	          |         |
	          |         +  vars.tcl (contains all varibles of the flow)
	          |         |
	          |         \  run_voltus.tcl (The consolidated flattened VOLTUS script to run the Analysis)
	          |
(Analysis O/Ps)   \  RPT  (Contains VOLTUS Analysis Output Reports)
	              |
	              +  static_power  (Static Power Reports)
	              |
	              +  static_rail  (Static Rail Analysis Reports)
	              |
	              +  dynamic_power (Dynamic Power and Ruch Current Analysis Reports)
	              |
	              \  dynamic_rail  (Dynamic Rail Analysis and Decap optimization Analysis Reports)

===============================
How to use the Foundation Flow:
===============================

1. Modify the following files before generating the code for VOLTUS Analysis.
        a. Copy the content in ./TEMPLATES/ to your run directory:
           >> cp -r ./TEMPLATES/VOLTUS/* <Run_directory>
	b. Modify "setup.tcl" with the design information. You can edit this file to set up the design file variables.
	c. Modify "voltus_config.tcl" with required voltus flow information. If the flows defined in it can't meet customers' need, enable plug-ins variables in the end of the file to customize. 
        d. (Optional) If you enable any plug-in in the previous step, you need to copy the plug-in directory to your run directory:
	  >> cp -r ./PLUG/ <Run_directory> 
	And then modify the corresponding plug-in files in PLUG/VOLTUS/ . Keep in mind that you need to add full VOLTUS commands in those appropriate plug-in files for the controls which were not covered in present "voltus_config.tcl"
	NOTE: You can change your plug-in directory with the variable vars(plug_root).

2. After the completion of the above step (step-1), use the following command to generate the flattened code.
	>> tclsh SCRIPTS/gen_voltus_flow.tcl
	This command generates the "FF/VOLTUS" directory in the run directory. This directory contains the flattened VOLTUS Foundation Flow scripts to run the flow. This command also generates the "Makefile" to run the flow. Check the "FF/voltus.check.rpt" file for the setup status. If this code generation report file ends with "Setup Check Passed", you can proceed with the next step. You can also browse the "FF/VOLTUS/run_voltus.tcl" to understand how and when the plug-in is applied.
	NOTE: The FF will detect most of the errors in the variables you defined, and error out in this step.  

3. Once the directory "FF" is ready after the above step (step-2), use the following command to run the ultimate Flow.
	a. Run the VOLTUS analysis on the design for the analysis set in the "voltus_config.tcl" file
	  >> make flow  
	NOTE: You can also run the optional command "make help" to show the usage of the "make flow". Now Makefile.voltus is automatically linked to Makefile

4. Results, The Outputs of the above step (step-3) will be under the following directories.
	a. LOG --> Contains the VOLTUS log reports
	b. RPT --> Contains all the VOLTUS Analysis Output Reports

============================
Update History -- 14.1
============================
1. New avariable list (Please refer to the comment lines for each usage):
	vars(generate_pg)
	vars(pg_only)
	vars(<domain1>,analyze_pwr_nets) 
	vars(<domain2>,analyze_gnd_nets) 
	vars(rail_extraction_tech_file)
	<A series of avariables for PG library generation>
	
2. Add PG library generation flow:
	If vars(generate_pg) = "false" and vars(pg_only) = "false", the FF will function as the old FF did.
	If vars(generate_pg) = "true" and vars(pg_only) = "false",  the FF will support PG library generation, all defined variables will be checked. The generated PG library will be used in the later flow to analyze power/rail.
	If vars(generate_pg) = "true" and vars(pg_only) = "true",  the FF will enter PG library generation only flow. This flow will only generate PG library, the further analysis will not proceed.

	If vars(techonly_pg_creation) = "true", techonly PG library will be generated based on the defined variables.
	If vars(stdcells_pg_creation)  = "true", stdcells PG library will be generated based on the defined variables.
	If vars(macros_pg_creation) = "true", macros PG library will be generated based on the defined variables.

3. Default changes:
	Default value of vars(dynamic_rail,accuracy)/var(static_rail,accuracy) is "hd" now according to the Voltus flow change.
